  '//! The bounds card. Quarry examples are compiled by tests/guide.rs.\n' +
    '// HV web figures: reports/20260929-hv-heavy-acquisition/REPORT.md, five-run table.\n' +
    'pub(super) const CARD: &str = r##"# Bounds and the meter\n' +
    '\n' +
    'The meter limits the work each read, mutation and job transaction can do.\n' +
    'Declare product limits; the engine chooses execution bounds within those ceilings.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '```quarry\n' +
    'table scalePosts:\n' +
    '  body: text <=500\n' +
    '  public\n' +
    '  online only\n' +
    'query scalePage(c: cursor ?):\n' +
    '  return scalePosts first 20 by .id after c\n' +
    'query scalePopulation():\n' +
    '  return count(scalePosts)\n' +
    '```\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Write product limits: a page size, a text length, an asset size or a real\n' +
    'per-group cap. Do not choose an index, a merge width or a job transaction\n' +
    'size. Predicate reads and views choose their plans; top-level job `for`\n' +
    'loops choose their chunks. Removing a written number never removes the meter.\n' +
    '\n' +
    "A query's `for row in t where .owner = viewer:` and a merge lane's source may omit `first N`\n" +
    'when the read rule is uniformly decided by that prefix; they read ascending\n' +
    'until the prefix ends or the meter cuts, and `check --cost` prints `rows ≤ meter`\n' +
    'and `lanes ≤ meter` when no fitting schema cap supplies a static bound.\n' +
    'A loop the meter cuts has no continuation; a total over a group that can outgrow one read is a maintained `view`.\n' +
    'A returned or bound page instead needs a schema cap or an explicit page bound.\n' +
    "Jobs may iterate uncapped domains under the chunk's meter. Top-level job\n" +
    '`for` sweeps shrink their transaction size after a meter refusal. Mutation loops\n' +
    'still need a schema-capped group that fits the examined ceiling. Direct\n' +
    '`count(domain)`, `sum(domain, .column)` and `exists domain` stream under the\n' +
    'meter without retaining the page. Schema-capped query `count` and `sum` with\n' +
    'non-uniform read rules keep their bounded page execution and coverage contract.\n' +
    'Mutations retain their uniform-read and\n' +
    'plain-prefix admission rules; a cut aborts the transaction, never commits a\n' +
    'partial total. A streaming query total with a meter cut or unknown device\n' +
    'coverage leaves the client read `loading`, never a partial count or sum.\n' +
    'Unknown earlier reads also make a streaming scalar unavailable, including\n' +
    'inputs saved in locals or used as domain bounds; a fallback cannot establish\n' +
    'coverage.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Allocation and completeness\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Heap is a cumulative allocation and binding budget. Streaming aggregates\n' +
    'release each transient row and its key scratch; one cursor allowance remains.\n' +
    'Inner job domains decode one prepaid row at a time and retain each selected\n' +
    "row under the heap meter before fetching another. Once decoded, the row's\n" +
    'retained allowance replaces its decode scratch. Retained rows, their vector\n' +
    'and the live cursor stay charged; domains do not retain unused result keys.\n' +
    'Constructed values,\n' +
    'concatenation and other allocating builtins, local bindings, and owned\n' +
    "copies count. Inspecting a held value's length or sum borrows it; row and\n" +
    'map clones share their immutable image. A heap cut stops a query immediately\n' +
    'with no available value or continuation, since an interrupted scalar or shape\n' +
    'has no valid partial answer. The client read is `loading`; narrow the query or\n' +
    'use a maintained view for a total. Its cut site remains internal;\n' +
    "the meter is available only through dev's default read inspection (CLIENT-AND-OPERATIONS.md §4).\n" +
    'An unfinished maintained lookup or live aggregate uses the same unavailable\n' +
    'query result, preserving zero only for a completed missing-group lookup.\n' +
    'A mutation rolls back; Operations below describes the refusal.\n' +
    'A page whose read rule the prefix does not decide (the deciding fields include a\n' +
    'column the scan does not pin) is never `complete`: the server cannot tell\n' +
    '"no more" from "more you may not see". Pin the deciding columns in the predicate, or read the page on the device (`guide sync`), where the\n' +
    'partition holds exactly what the viewer may read. `check` says so\n' +
    '(`N_NEVER_COMPLETE`), as it notes a query page returned without a cursor\n' +
    '(`N_NO_CURSOR`), a synced table whose groups can grow with no horizon\n' +
    '(`N_NO_HORIZON`), and a merge past 50 lanes (`N_WIDE_MERGE`).\n' +
    '`complete` means the query answered its declared request within known coverage and execution limits.\n' +
    'Filling `first N` or `last N` is complete, including a composed preview.\n' +
    'A cursorless page cannot continue; declare `c: cursor ?` and use `after c`\n' +
    'if the screen pages. Composed fields and pages covering a fitting group cap\n' +
    'omit `N_NO_CURSOR`.\n' +
    '\n' +
    '## Operations\n' +
    '\n' +
    'Nothing is priced at check. As a program runs, the meter counts examined\n' +
