    'query past a ceiling returns what it found with `complete: false`; a\n' +
    'mutation aborts with E_BOUND naming the meter, the ceiling and the site\n' +
    '(never the count: it would measure rows the viewer may not read).\n' +
    'Read a smaller page, narrow its predicate, or move the sweep into a job.\n' +
    'Authorization-dependent scans prepay a fixed logical allowance before row\n' +
    "discovery. Hidden candidates do not consume the caller's remaining allowance;\n" +
    'readable rows, filters and output still do. These logical meters exclude private\n' +
    'scan work: authorization candidates share one physical limit of 8,192\n' +
    'per request, including nested witnesses and maintained-source walks. A row behind at least 8,192 such candidates is unreachable by paging\n' +
    'in that direction; an empty page has no cursor into the hidden range. Expiring\n' +
    'cap checks draw from that same allowance; any authorization that cannot be\n' +
    'established within it returns generic E_RULE without identifying a cause.\n' +
    "The device's separate prediction-work budget can instead queue an operation.\n" +
    "`snapback4 check --cost` prints each site's structural class;\n" +
    '`snapback4 test` prints the numbers on your data and names query/persona reads\n' +
    'past half any ceiling without a cut: at most ten lines and a count of the rest.\n' +
    'Loopback `dev` logs actual meter and word cuts with the operation, principal,\n' +
